03:22.280 --> 03:32.540
partitioned parameter A and the second partitioned parameter B respectively. Now, after we computed

03:32.540 --> 03:38.760
the Jacobian in the partitioned way, we can put it together into the normal equation to

03:38.760 --> 03:44.660
compute J transpose J, which is this guy over here, and we will see that it has a very nice

03:44.660 --> 03:52.500
structure over here. And delta would also have a partitioned structure where the first

03:52.500 --> 03:59.280
set of this vector would be representing A, and the second set would be representing the

03:59.280 --> 04:05.060
delta increment of B. And similarly, for the right side of this normal equation, which

04:05.060 --> 04:11.700
is given by minus J transpose of epsilon, we can see that the structure would also be

04:11.700 --> 04:17.620
the first part here is only dependent on the parameters of A, and the second part will

