the first entry of y, and then solve for this first entry, and gradually do a back substitution

27:40.100 --> 27:47.620
to solve for all the other entries in y. So once we have obtained y over here, we can see that

27:47.620 --> 27:53.060
y is actually equal to U and x. We'll solve for another homogeneous linear equation where

27:53.060 --> 28:01.940
this becomes an upper triangular matrix. So what we will have here would be an upper triangular

28:01.940 --> 28:10.980
matrix over here multiplied by x, where y is now a known value. We can do a back substitution,

28:10.980 --> 28:14.660
solve for the first value over here that corresponds to the last element of x,

28:14.660 --> 28:20.820
and do a back substitution to solve for all the elements over here. Similarly, we can also apply

28:20.820 --> 28:27.380
the QR decomposition and the Cholesky decomposition, where QR decomposition here

28:27.380 --> 28:33.620
simply means that the Q matrix is an octagonal matrix, and the inverse of an octagonal matrix

28:33.620 --> 28:39.780
is simply the transpose. So we can solve for this as QR multiplied by x equals to B,

28:39.780 --> 28:47.060
and then we can do a Rx equals to Q transpose or B, which can be easily computed by taking

28:47.060 --> 28:53.300
the transpose. We do not need the inverse of this, which is easier to compute in this case.

28:53.300 --> 28:58.500
So once we have computed this, then we'll end up with another system or linear equation,

28:58.500 --> 29:06.100
which we call this collectively as y. We will end up having to solve Rx equals to y,

29:06.100 --> 29:11.940
where R here is a lower or upper triangular matrix that we can take advantage of the same

29:12.500 --> 29:19.060
method to solve for the unknowns of x over here. And similarly for Cholesky decomposition,

29:19.060 --> 29:25.380
which is probably the most commonly used decomposition or factorization technique

29:25.380 --> 29:31.300
to solve for the normal equation in the Loevenberg-Markov algorithm, where we simply

29:31.540 --> 29:39.540
factorize A into a square root matrix L multiplied by L transpose, where L here

29:40.660 --> 29:48.500
is a lower triangular matrix that we can then solve for the x in the similar way as

29:49.460 --> 29:55.300
what we have seen in the LU factorization. For more information about this, because you should

29:55.300 --> 30:01.940
have learned this in your undergraduate Linear Algebra course, I won't go through in very much

