30:52.420 --> 30:59.380
Now unfortunately, the normal equation cannot be solved in a naive way of just

30:59.380 --> 31:07.060
taking the LU decomposition, Cholesky decomposition, or other form of decomposition,

31:07.060 --> 31:16.420
because we'll more than often face what we call the problem of fill-in in this kind of factorization

31:16.420 --> 31:22.980
techniques. So what it means here is that if I were to have a matrix A in the homogeneous

31:22.980 --> 31:31.300
linear equation of A X equals to B, I would, one technique that I have mentioned earlier on here

31:31.300 --> 31:37.540
