32:11.140 --> 32:18.500
back substitution steps. And one way to resolve this is to reorder the sparse matrix of A by a

32:18.500 --> 32:27.860
permutation matrix. So permutation matrix simply means a matrix that is with entries of 1 or 0

32:27.860 --> 32:35.940
in the matrix, and every column and every row of this particular matrix has to sum up to 1.

32:35.940 --> 32:43.780
So this means that I have to have only 1 once in a particular row as well as a particular

