this is what we will get. We will still get the same number of non-zero elements because we are

35:36.100 --> 35:43.620
simply reordering the entries in the sparse matrix of A. And after applying Kolosky decomposition,

35:43.620 --> 35:54.340
we can see that we are, we end up to have 52,988 non-zero elements over here. This is still much

